# Keep the Docker build context small. The backend/web Dockerfiles run a fresh
# `pnpm install` inside the image, so host node_modules / build output must NOT
# be shipped to the daemon (they are huge and OS-specific).
**/node_modules
.git
.github
.pnpm-store
**/.next
**/.expo
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/coverage
# ...but NOT the dashboard's "Coverage map" route page, which lives at
# apps/web-dashboard/app/coverage/ and was being wrongly excluded by the line above
# (caused /coverage to 404 in the Docker web image).
!apps/web-dashboard/app/coverage
!apps/web-dashboard/app/coverage/**
**/*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
graphify-out
docs
infra/erpnext-crm
apps/desktop-operations/release
apps/mobile-field-sales/android
apps/mobile-field-sales/ios
.codex-run
.claude
